            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed both added files in full. Check validates feature and head (review.CheckFeature, review.CheckRev) before any git or store call, so option-like heads and path-traversal features do not reach git or the filesystem; engine/review/app/check_test.go covers both.",
              "Stored results are re-parsed and held to their binding (judged), the candidate is recomputed from git for the stored base and delivered head, and review.CheckBinding must match. A forged base is rejected as invalid stored before git is asked, per the test TestCheckDoesNotPassAForgedBaseToGit.",
              "Verdict handling fails closed: only ErrNotFound is treated as no verdict; any other read or parse error is a refusal. Severe findings without a verdict are not clear per the tests.",
              "Check writes nothing to the store, and all git/store failures are returned as refusals, so no data loss or exposure path is introduced. No secrets or dependency changes appear in the patch."
            ]
          }
        }
