            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Check validates the feature and head before any git or store call. Every failure path (locate, resolve head, list, read, parse, bind, binding mismatch, verdict read or parse) returns an error with an empty Checked, so it fails closed. The tests assert this with errors.Is, message content, an empty result and an unchanged store write count.",
              "A verdict that is missing (ErrNotFound) is distinguished from one that is unreadable or invalid. The unreadable-verdict test and the unknown-ID verdict case cover this.",
              "Results of a commit whose name shares only the first 12 characters are filtered by the stored Head. The collision test covers this, and the order of launches 2 and 10 is asserted regardless of listing order.",
              "The forged-base test asserts that git is never given an option-like revision. The git call sequence and store call sequence are asserted exactly for the happy path.",
              "I found no defect caused by this candidate. Remaining observations are minor: the VerdictName error is returned without path context, and I could not see the fake helpers."
            ]
          }
        }
